---
description: Conventions for all code in this repo
alwaysApply: true
---
- Python 3.12, pytest. Money is `decimal.Decimal`, never float. Dates are `datetime.date`.
- Keep business logic in pure functions with no database access. Keep database access in a thin adapter.
- Do not edit: `sql/`, `golden/`, `api/contract/openapi.json`, `slack-drop/`, `.cursor/`, `legacy/`.
- Never add DDL: no new tables, columns, indexes or functions. Use the existing tables only.
- The HTTP contract in `api/contract/openapi.json` must not change. `pytest api/tests` must pass.
- Before you open a pull request:
  1. `pytest` passes.
  2. The parity command given in the task prompt has been run, and its summary line is in the PR description.
- PR title starts with `[conversion]`, `[tool]` or `[label]`. PR body has four headings:
  What changed, Tests run, Parity result, Open questions.
- Do not stop at the first failing parity case. Report every difference you could not explain under Open questions.
